<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23577" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">innŭbus</span></b> , a, um, adj.
		2. in-nubo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>unmarried.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 10,
				567</span></i>; <i><span class="en">14, 142</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pallas,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Epigr. 106</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Val.
				Fl. 1, 87</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">diva,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 4,
					605</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, of the laurel (because Daphne, who
			was never married, was changed into it): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">innuba laurus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					10, 92</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
